{
 "construct": "dawn",
 "name": "Dawn",
 "about": "Dawn from Cape Canaveral to Vesta and Ceres. Its ion engines thrust for most of the cruise, so in place of big burns the log keeps Horizons' osculating orbit about the Sun every few months, the Mars flyby of 2009, and its orbits at Vesta (2011 to 2012) and Ceres (2015 to 2018), where it fell silent on 31 Oct 2018 and still orbits. Arrival and departure dates follow the Horizons header; their hours are from memory.",
